  "prefLabel": "Env-A 609.04 Insignificant Activities",
  "priorExpiration": "2011-10-24",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 609.04 Insignificant Activities.\n\n(a) A list of insignificant activities shall be included in an application for a title V operating permit.\n\n(b) Emissions from activities identified as insignificant activities in (d), below shall be quantified.\n\n(c) Insignificant activities shall be subject to emission-based fees specified in Env-A 705.\n\n(d) A device, source, or activity that is not an exempt activity under Env-A 609.03 shall be classified as an insignificant activity if it:\n\n(1) Is below any applicable threshold specified in Env-A 607.01;\n\n(2) Emits less than 1,000 lbs. per year of all regulated air pollutants, other than GHGs, in aggregate; and\n\n(3) Emits less than 200 tons per year of CO2e.\n\nSource. #6057-B, eff 6-30-95; ss by #7879, eff 4-26-03; amd by #8129, eff 7-28-04; amd by #9906, INTERIM, eff 4-26-11, EXPIRES: 10-24-11; ss by #10000, eff 10-1-11; ss by #10175, eff 9-1-12; ss by #13510, eff 12-17-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a600.html"
